  "claim": "The star of \"The Green Carriage\" played in one of the works Anastasiya Vertinskaya came to prominence with in the early 1960s. His character was summoned by King Carolyne zu Sayn-Wittgenstein to distract the prince from his apparent madness.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Igor Dmitriev. Sentence: Igor Borisovich Dmitriev (Russian: И́горь Бори́сович Дми́триев ) (May 29, 1927 – January 26, 2008) was a Russian film and theater actor who specialized in playing aristocratic characters in costume productions (e.g., Rosencrantz in Grigori Kozintsev's \"Hamlet\").\nPage: Rosencrantz and Guildenstern. Sentence: They are childhood friends of Hamlet, summoned by King Claudius to distract the prince from his apparent madness and if possible to ascertain the cause of it.\nPage: The Green Carriage. Sentence: The Green Carriage (Russian: Зелёная карета , \"Zelyonaya kareta \" ) is a 1967 Soviet historical drama film directed by Yan Frid and starring Natalya Tenyakova, Vladimir Chestnokov and Igor Dmitriev.\nPage: Anastasiya Vertinskaya. Sentence: Anastasiya Alexandrovna Vertinskaya (Russian: Анастаси́я Алекса́ндровна Верти́нская , born 19 December 1944, Moscow, Soviet Union), is a Soviet and Russian actress, who came to prominence in the early 1960s with her acclaimed performances in \"Scarlet Sails\", \"Amphibian Man\" and Grigori Kozintsev's \"Hamlet\".",
  "evidence_text": "Page: Igor Dmitriev. Sentence: Igor Borisovich Dmitriev (Russian: И́горь Бори́сович Дми́триев ) (May 29, 1927 – January 26, 2008) was a Russian film and theater actor who specialized in playing aristocratic characters in costume productions (e.g., Rosencrantz in Grigori Kozintsev's \"Hamlet\").\nPage: Rosencrantz and Guildenstern. Sentence: They are childhood friends of Hamlet, summoned by King Claudius to distract the prince from his apparent madness and if possible to ascertain the cause of it.\nPage: The Green Carriage. Sentence: The Green Carriage (Russian: Зелёная карета , \"Zelyonaya kareta \" ) is a 1967 Soviet historical drama film directed by Yan Frid and starring Natalya Tenyakova, Vladimir Chestnokov and Igor Dmitriev.\nPage: Anastasiya Vertinskaya. Sentence: Anastasiya Alexandrovna Vertinskaya (Russian: Анастаси́я Алекса́ндровна Верти́нская , born 19 December 1944, Moscow, Soviet Union), is a Soviet and Russian actress, who came to prominence in the early 1960s with her acclaimed performances in \"Scarlet Sails\", \"Amphibian Man\" and Grigori Kozintsev's \"Hamlet\".",
