        "original_id": "44ca5c37-5eda-58f5-9ebd-84191627bb9a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Igor Dmitriev, Anastasiya Vertinskaya\n- Films: Hamlet, The Green Carriage, Scarlet Sails, Amphibian Man\n- Fictional Characters: Rosencrantz, Guildenstern, Hamlet, King Claudius\n- Directors: Grigori Kozintsev, Yan Frid\n\nFacts:\n- Igor Dmitriev was born on May 29, 1927, and he died on January 26, 2008.\n- Anastasiya Vertinskaya was born on December 19, 1944, in Moscow, Soviet Union.\n- Anastasiya Vertinskaya came to prominence in the early 1960s through her performances in Scarlet Sails, Amphibian Man, and Grigori Kozintsev's Hamlet.\n- The Green Carriage is a 1967 Soviet historical drama film directed by Yan Frid and starring Natalya Tenyakova, Vladimir Chestnokov, and Igor Dmitriev.\n- Igor Dmitriev was a Russian film and theater actor known for playing aristocratic characters in costume productions, including Rosencrantz in Grigori Kozintsev's Hamlet.\n- Rosencrantz and Guildenstern are childhood friends of Hamlet who are summoned by King Claudius to distract Hamlet from his apparent madness and discover its cause.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "f52dfa18-049b-51b7-a7ce-7b52ad58286d",
        "text": "Page: Igor Dmitriev. Sentence: Igor Borisovich Dmitriev (Russian: И́горь Бори́сович Дми́триев ) (May 29, 1927 – January 26, 2008) was a Russian film and theater actor who specialized in playing aristocratic characters in costume productions (e.g., Rosencrantz in Grigori Kozintsev's \"Hamlet\").\nPage: Rosencrantz and Guildenstern. Sentence: They are childhood friends of Hamlet, summoned by King Claudius to distract the prince from his apparent madness and if possible to ascertain the cause of it.\nPage: The Green Carriage. Sentence: The Green Carriage (Russian: Зелёная карета , \"Zelyonaya kareta \" ) is a 1967 Soviet historical drama film directed by Yan Frid and starring Natalya Tenyakova, Vladimir Chestnokov and Igor Dmitriev.\nPage: Anastasiya Vertinskaya. Sentence: Anastasiya Alexandrovna Vertinskaya (Russian: Анастаси́я Алекса́ндровна Верти́нская , born 19 December 1944, Moscow, Soviet Union), is a Soviet and Russian actress, who came to prominence in the early 1960s with her acclaimed performances in \"Scarlet Sails\", \"Amphibian Man\" and Grigori Kozintsev's \"Hamlet\".",
